course: dictionary
lesson: 12157
title: Complainer: a person who grumbles
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A complainer is a person who complains a lot. The ending -er means someone who does the action, like a reader reads or a singer sings. «Our class complainer moans every time we have fish for lunch.» The writer thinks this child grumbles too much, so the word is used as criticism.
explain: The word has a second meaning, which grown-ups use more. A complainer can also be a person who makes an official complaint, for example to a shop or a council. «The council wrote back to the complainer within a week.» Here the word is neutral. It just means someone who has made a formal complaint.
explain: Use the clues around the word. Words like «moans» and «every time» tell you about someone who grumbles often. Words like «council» and «wrote back» tell you the second meaning. Ask yourself: does this person grumble, or have they made an official complaint?
fact: Complainer means a person who complains a lot, often about small things.
fact: Complainer can also mean a person who makes an official complaint.
fact: A complainer often grumbles about food, weather or rules.
fact: Similar words: «moaner», «grump» and «whinger» (UK and Australia).
fact: The ending -er shows a person who does something: complain becomes complainer.
exercise: «Our class complainer moans every time we have fish for lunch.» What does complainer mean here? | A person who likes fish very much | A person who cooks the school lunch | *A person who always grumbles, often about small things | A person who is always late
exercise: «The council wrote back to the complainer within a week.» What does complainer mean here? | A person who wrote a book | A person who grumbles about food | *A person who made an official complaint | A council worker who cooks
exercise: Which word is a similar word for complainer? | Rainbow | Library | Bridge | *Grump
test: The shop manager spoke kindly to the complainer who had brought back a broken toaster. What is a complainer? | A person who sells toasters | A person who eats toast every morning | A person who mends toasters | *A person who makes a complaint
test: Why might someone call a classmate a complainer? | Because they never say a word | *Because they grumble about small things all the time | Because they have a loud laugh | Because they won every race
exam: Which of these is NOT a meaning of complainer? | A person who makes an official complaint | *A person who builds bridges | A person who grumbles about rules | A person who complains a lot
